# SABOTAGE: WS-NOTES Phase 3 unit 3.13 — THE PAGE IS DELETED AND ITS SUBPAGES ARE NOT
# `Doc` attaches `CascadeArchive` so deleting a page retires its whole subtree (one instant, one
# `record_archived` row per page). This patch un-attaches the change: the page leaves the tree, its
# `record_archived` row lands, the parent's content survives, and every subpage is still LIVE —
# pointing at a parent no read can see. That is the orphan: the child cannot be reached from its
# ancestor, and it is not in the trash either, so nobody can find it to delete or restore it.
#
# Silent everywhere the tree is one level deep: the list renders, the trash lists, the purge works.
# Only a delete of a page that HAS children distinguishes the two.
#
# Aimed at the MODEL attachment only. `CascadeRestore`, the purge's subtree walk and the surfaces
# are untouched.
#
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/notes_tree_cascade_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: the whole subtree leaves the tree, each page audited, all at one instant
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/docs/blueprint.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/docs/blueprint.ex
@@ -190,7 +190,6 @@
           # needs `on: [:destroy]` explicitly or it silently never runs (`Cms`/`Support` say the
           # same at their own attachment). It then also reaches the plain `:destroy` and
           # `:destroy_permanently`, which the name guard skips.
-          change(Samen.Scopes.Docs.CascadeArchive, on: [:destroy])
           change(Samen.Scopes.Docs.CascadeRestore)
         end
 
